Screened 100 studies (indices 1-100) for the systematic review on diagnostic accuracy of visual inspection and 
dermoscopy for BCC and cSCC in adults. Result: 18 studies INCLUDED, 82 studies EXCLUDED.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
Total studies screened: 100
Included: 18 studies
Excluded: 82 studies

INCLUDED STUDIES (18):
- Study 12: "Accuracy of clinical diagnosis of skin lesions" - Evaluates clinical diagnostic accuracy for BCC (72.7% 
PPV) and SCC (49.4% PPV) with histological confirmation.
- Study 21: "Differences in dermoscopic images from nonpolarized dermoscope and polarized dermoscope" - Compares 
polarized vs nonpolarized dermoscopy including 3 BCCs with histological reference.
- Study 31: "Can video thermography improve differential diagnosis and therapy between basal cell carcinoma and actinic 
keratosis?" - Compares video thermography with dermoscopy for BCC diagnosis.
- Study 32: "Accuracy and predictors of basal cell carcinoma diagnosis" - Evaluates clinical diagnostic accuracy for BCC
with histological confirmation (80% PPV).
- Study 36: "Dermoscopy of squamous cell carcinoma and keratoacanthoma" - Characterizes dermoscopic criteria for SCC and
keratoacanthoma with histological confirmation.
- Study 44: "Modified dermoscopic algorithm for the differentiation between melanocytic and nonmelanocytic skin tumors" 
- Evaluates dermoscopic algorithms including BCC differentiation with histological confirmation.
- Study 46: "Prospective study of the accuracy of the surgeon's diagnosis in 2000 excised skin tumors" - Evaluates 
clinical diagnosis accuracy for skin tumors including BCC/SCC with histology.
- Study 53: "Decision support software to help primary care physicians triage skin cancer: a pilot study" - Evaluates 
decision support for BCC/SCC triage with histological confirmation.
- Study 58: "Evaluation of optical coherence tomography as a means of identifying earlier stage basal cell carcinomas" -
Includes clinical and dermoscopic evaluation for BCC with histological confirmation.
- Study 63: "The sensitivity and specificity of optical coherence tomography for the assisted diagnosis of nonpigmented 
basal cell carcinoma" - Includes clinical assessment and dermoscopy for BCC with histological confirmation.
- Study 71: "Assessment of SIAscopy in the triage of suspicious skin tumours" - Compares SIAscopy with 
clinical-dermoscopic diagnosis including BCC with histological confirmation.
- Study 72: "Dermatoscopy of basal cell carcinoma: morphologic variability of global and local features and accuracy of 
diagnosis" - Investigates dermatoscopic features of BCC (609 BCCs) with histological confirmation.
- Study 75: "Mobile teledermatology for skin tumour screening" - Evaluates clinical and dermoscopic tele-evaluation 
including 58 malignant nonmelanocytic lesions (BCC/SCC) with histological confirmation.
- Study 87: "Diagnosing basal cell carcinoma by dermatoscopy" - Determines dermatoscopic features of nonpigmented BCC 
with histological confirmation.
- Study 91: "Use of the mobile phone multimedia messaging service for teledermatology" - Evaluates teledermatology for 
skin tumours with histopathological diagnosis.
- Study 95: "Dermoscopy improves accuracy of primary care physicians to triage lesions suggestive of skin cancer" - 
Evaluates dermoscopy for skin cancer triage with histopathologic confirmation.
- Study 96: "A comparison of diagnosis, evaluation, and treatment of patients with dermatologic disorders" - Compares 
diagnosis accuracy of PCPs vs dermatologists with histological confirmation.
- Study 97: "Diagnostic accuracy for skin cancer: comparison of general practitioner with dermatologist and 
dermatopathologist" - Examines diagnostic accuracy for skin cancer with histological confirmation.

EXCLUDED STUDIES (82):
Primary exclusion reasons:
- Melanoma-focused studies (majority): Studies evaluating melanoma diagnosis only (e.g., studies 1-5, 7-10, 13-17, 
19-20, 22-23, 25-29, 34, 37-39, 41-43, 47-52, 54-56, 59-62, 64, 66, 67, 69, 73-74, 76, 78-80, 83-86, 89-90, 93, 98-100)
- Systematic reviews/meta-analyses: Studies 18, 30, 35, 48, 68, 94
- Review articles: Studies 45, 70, 77, 82
- Case reports: Studies 6, 11
- Treatment studies: Studies 40, 65
- Intervention/training studies: Studies 3, 78
- Screening campaigns: Studies 8, 69, 84
- Methodological studies: Studies 24, 57, 88
- Trial protocols: Study 79
- Non-skin cancer studies: Study 92 (UTI)
- Epidemiology studies: Study 33, 81, 94

### 3. Additional context:
The screening was conducted based on the selection criteria: "Studies of any design that evaluated visual inspection or 
dermoscopy or both in adults with lesions suspicious for skin cancer, compared with a reference standard of either 
histological confirmation or clinical follow-up."

Key inclusion criteria applied:
1. Must evaluate visual inspection or dermoscopy (or both)
2. Must include BCC or cSCC (not just melanoma)
3. Must have histological confirmation or clinical follow-up as reference standard
4. Must be a diagnostic accuracy study (not treatment, review, or protocol)

Studies were conservatively included when they evaluated dermoscopy or visual inspection for BCC/cSCC even if they also 
included other skin cancers. Studies focused exclusively on melanoma were excluded as they do not address the review 
objective of BCC and cSCC detection.

