Conclusions  Dermoscopy reduced the number of excisions, but did not improve the detection of melanomas. Our results    
suggest that in everyday clinical practice of general dermatologists the main contribution of dermoscopy is a reduction 
of unnecessary excisions.Oxford University Press"}, {"study_index": 100, "title": "Spectrophotometric intracutaneous    
