Dermoscopy greatly improves the clinical diagnosis of pigmented lesions. Few studies have investigated, however, how 
dermoscopy is guiding management decisions in everyday clinical practice. In addition, most studies have been performed 
in the setting of dermoscopy experts working in pigmented lesion clinics.                    Objectives  To assess the 
impact of dermoscopy on clinical diagnosis and management decisions for pigmented lesions in everyday practice of 
general dermatologists.                    Methods  We performed a prospective study in general dermatology clinics in 
