on melanoma detection using dermoscopy or other imaging modalities, which falls outside the scope of this review 
targeting keratinocyte cancers.\n\n2. Treatment studies: Several studies evaluated treatment outcomes for BCC or SCC 
(e.g., imiquimod vs surgery, vismodegib therapy) but did not assess diagnostic accuracy.\n\n3. Educational 
interventions: Multiple studies assessed training programs or educational modules for improving diagnostic skills, which
are not diagnostic accuracy studies per se.\n\n4. Alternative imaging modalities: Studies focusing on RCM, MPT/FLIM, 
SIAscopy, or computer-aided diagnosis without evaluating visual inspection or dermoscopy were excluded.\n\nCONSERVATIVE 
SCREENING APPROACH:\nStudies that included both melanoma and keratinocyte cancers in their analysis were INCLUDED when 
they provided separable data or when the index test (dermoscopy/visual inspection) was evaluated against histological 
confirmation for keratinocyte cancers. This conservative approach ensures potentially relevant studies proceed to 
full-text review.'}
